WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-TR

00:00:03.621 --> 00:00:05.364
DeskPack for Adobe Photoshop brings

00:00:05.526 --> 00:00:08.361
your flexo expertise to your desktop,
along with your favorite retouching application

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.681
.

00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:14.953
With Viewer, you can view a color-accurate preview of your image, whether it will be printed with process inks,
spot inks, or a combination of

00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:17.229
both.


00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:19.521
 


00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:22.429
 
You see your image exactly as it will be printed, which reduces the need for

00:00:22.846 --> 00:00:25.241
intermediate test prints
.

00:00:26.003 --> 00:00:27.863
With a multi-channel densitometer, you can place multiple measurement points in

00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:30.008
critical areas of your image


00:00:30.171 --> 00:00:32.361
 
.

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:35.013
This provides you with numerical feedback when editing the image

00:00:35.173 --> 00:00:36.721
 
.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.241
Minimal dots and accent cuts
require special attention.

00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:46.561
Viewer
simulates this behavior on cliché and print to catch errors early.

00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:49.441
 
You can see where the gradations are broken

00:00:49.803 --> 00:00:53.801
and check how your images adapt correctly to your flexographic prints
.

00:00:54.351 --> 00:00:57.883
Viewer also highlights the Total Area Coverage,
or TAC, showing areas where the

00:00:58.184 --> 00:01:02.481
ink coverage of your image
exceeds a certain limit.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:05.481
This reduces problems during ink cutting, resulting in a


00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:09.041
cleaner printout and
fewer issues.

00:01:09.841 --> 00:01:13.881
Many of your images can be set aside for offset printing and
retouched.

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:17.841
But what if the same images need to be
printed using flexography?

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:21.961
FlexoFix
helps you convert your images for flexographic printing.  Unlike

00:01:22.653 --> 00:01:25.488
other curve or color management
approaches,

00:01:25.928 --> 00:01:28.113
FlexoFix analyzes your images

00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:30.948
and then applies context-sensitive
changes.

00:01:31.453 --> 00:01:33.681
This helps to resolve the most common problems while also


00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:37.681
 
preserving the accuracy and saturation of the image.  The

00:01:38.281 --> 00:01:42.321
FlexoClean filter
works like other filters in Photoshop.  It

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:44.961
automatically removes stains

00:01:45.124 --> 00:01:47.761
and fills small holes
with minimal spotting.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.923
With FlexoClean, your printing plates will be
cleaner and

00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:53.201
your print quality will be excellent.

00:01:53.881 --> 00:01:56.161
Your images
are prepared for process printing,

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:59.721
but your packaging will also use spot or
brand colors.  What happens if you replace

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:03.959
 


00:02:04.121 --> 00:02:06.401
some of your process inks with spot
inks without changing how the image appears?

00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:08.841
This is what InkSwitch
offers.  Based on

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:11.576
Esko color management,


00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:14.763
InkSwitch analyzes the entire gamut of your image


00:02:14.924 --> 00:02:17.881
and calculates


00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:19.881
a new set of spot color
separations that match the original image.

00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:23.681
InkSwitch is a spot
color tool for Photoshop.

00:02:24.273 --> 00:02:26.993
InkSwitch helps you keep the number of ink cartridges
to a minimum and

00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:28.896
reduces ink usage,


00:02:29.056 --> 00:02:31.081
 
saving you time and money.  You get better quality

00:02:31.726 --> 00:02:34.515
from your spot color images
:

00:02:34.861 --> 00:02:36.163
better color balance,

00:02:36.276 --> 00:02:39.600
better solid ink densities,
and better dot gain control.

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:41.828
With DeskPack for Photoshop,

00:02:41.988 --> 00:02:43.640
 
you can identify problems early,

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:46.601
reducing costs
and saving time.  Your

00:02:47.305 --> 00:02:49.794
learning curve is short and your training
costs are low

00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:54.361
because the look and feel of the plugins are the
same as the rest of Adobe Photoshop.  You can prepare

00:02:55.176 --> 00:02:58.081
your images for flexographic printing
faster, with

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.620
higher quality, and with fewer errors
.

00:03:01.261 --> 00:03:04.061
DeskPack for Photoshop
makes you an expert.

